// Smaller stand-in for `level_01.ron`'s 280x160 grid: 3x2 tiles instead of
// 44,800, each scaled 100x in X/Z (not Y, to avoid making a thin flat tile
// 100x thicker too) and spaced 100 apart so they still tile edge-to-edge -
// same total-footprint idea as the full grid, far fewer entities. Each tile
// carries its own `ColliderConstructor` sized to 1x0.1x1 (unscaled) rather
// than one collider spanning the whole grid - avian3d auto-scales a
// collider by the entity's own `Transform.scale` (confirmed in
// `avian3d::collision::collider::backend`: "Updates collider scale based on
// `Transform` scale"), so the same 100x scale already on each tile for the
// mesh stretches its collider to match, no separate entity needed.
//
// Also carries a character (entity 8) and third-person camera (entity 9),
// positioned near the grid's center - `Character`/`CharacterVisual`/
// `ThirdPersonCamera`/`CharacterAnimationState` only became reflectable once
// `Reflect`/`#[reflect(Component)]` were added to them in `components/mod.rs`.
// `InputMap` is deliberately NOT here - it's reflectable, but its fields are
// `HashMap<Action, Vec<Box<dyn Buttonlike>>>` (boxed trait objects), not
// something to hand-author - `attach_character_input` in
// `character_controller/mod.rs` attaches it in Rust instead, reactively,
// to whichever entity has `Character`/`Camera3d` regardless of where it
// came from.
//
// Known gaps:
// - No checkerboard tint (`StandardMaterial` has no RON-authorable form -
//   every tile renders with `ground_tile.glb`'s own baked-in material).
// - The character's visual mesh (entity 10) is here - same `WorldAssetRoot`
//   pointing at a glTF scene as every tile - but it's a standalone entity,
//   NOT a `ChildOf` the character. Avian3d's own docs say rigid-body
//   hierarchies are treated as flat ("moving the parent will not affect the
//   child... write your own system to handle hierarchies differently"), and
//   that's confirmed here: with `ChildOf` wired up, the mesh's
//   `GlobalTransform` never updated past its initial (wrong) value, even
//   after 15+ seconds. `sync_character_visual_transform` in
//   `character_controller/mod.rs` now does that sync manually every frame
//   instead of relying on hierarchy propagation.
// - Animated as of 2026-10-26: `character_controller::build_character_animation_graph`
//   loads 3 more glTF files (idle/walking/jumping) and builds an
//   `AnimationGraph` from clips spread across all of them at runtime - that
//   combination step has no RON equivalent, so it stays Rust, attached to
//   this mesh's `AnimationPlayer` once it appears (`attach_character_animation_graph`).
//   A `GameState::Loading`/`Playing` split (`components::GameState`) gates
//   gameplay until that - and everything else below - is actually ready.
(
  resources: {},
  entities: {
    1: (
      components: {
        "bevy_transform::components::transform::Transform": (
          translation: (0.0, 0.0, 0.0),
          rotation: (0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0),
          scale: (100.0, 1.0, 100.0),
        ),
        "bevy_world_serialization::components::WorldAssetRoot": (Path("models/terrain/ground_tile.glb#Scene0")),
        "RigidBody": Static,
        "ColliderConstructor": Cuboid(
          x_length: 1.0,
          y_length: 0.1,
          z_length: 1.0,
        ),
      },
    ),
    2: (
